invariant: INV-26
file: ct.h
catches: test/quic-builds.sh
reason: the suite build on the AES=soft table accepts
  CH_AES_EXTERN_CONSTANT_TIME in place of a host object or AES=extern. The
  flag is a statement about the peripheral behind ch_aes_block, and an
  AES=soft object calls no such hook: its traffic keys go to the S-box,
  which is indexed with the key, and nothing states anything about it
  (docs/decisions.md 68). quic-builds.sh compiles the suite on AES=soft
  with the extern flag alone and requires ct.h to refuse it.

--- old
#if !defined(CH_CPU_RUNTIME) && !defined(CH_AES_EXTERN)
--- new
#if !defined(CH_CPU_RUNTIME) && !defined(CH_AES_EXTERN) && !defined(CH_AES_EXTERN_CONSTANT_TIME)
